{"ts":"2026-11-15T01:31:09.749Z","actor":"claude","stage":"factcheck","action":"factcheck.review","details":{"verdict":"pass","notes":"NASA (What Is Microgravity, grades 5-8): ISS at 200–250 miles (320–400 km; 'about 400 km' is the upper end and matches typical ISS altitude); gravity about 90% of the surface value; astronauts float because they are in free fall, falling toward but around Earth; 17,500 mph = 28,164 km/h ('about 28,000'). NASA Glenn: 'many people mistakenly think gravity does not exist in space'. The title states the truth, so the hook does not reinforce the myth. Photos are captioned by NASA (ISS 2018, Meir with a water sphere 2020)."},"gitSha":"1e0af98"}
